DENCE`) resolved\n  automatically, exactly as `unit_graph.register_unit_path` was already\n  designed to do, once D16-D23's bodies entered the bindings it receives —\n  confirmed by compiling and inspecting the real graph, not by re-reading\n  source (see \"Compiled-graph proof\" below).\n\n**P-N31-002 correction**: generation 2/3's own result report used a\nmalformed multi-line `status:` field with a trailing parenthetical, which\nthe controller's `^status:\\s*(PASSED|NOT_AVAILABLE|BLOCKED)\\s*$` parser\ncannot match. Fixed to a bare `status: PASSED` line (above); the caveat that\nparenthetical was capturing — stale N20/N30 fixtures — was independently\nresolved by P-N20-001/P-N30-001, and both of this node's required\nverification commands are reconfirmed green below.\n\n**P-N31-003 correction**: generation 3's honest `BLOCKED` report (per\nP-N31-002's own instruction to report a real residual failure rather than\nforce a `PASSED` status) named two `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` failures that\nwere structural *consequences* of this node's own D16-D23 wiring. Both are\nnow closed, in `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` only, nothing else in that file\ntouched:\n\n1. `test_the_unobservable_boundary_is_excluded_for_a_stated_reason` — its\n   docstring pre-assigned this rewrite to N31: before D16-D23 were wired,\n   M05's own stream update was swallowed because the branch reaching it\n   resolved to the still-deferred `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE` and aborted the\n   superstep. With D16 now a real node body, M05's update is genuinely\n   observable, so the test now asserts that inversion directly (a real,\n   non-empty `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE`-preceding stream chunk for\n   `UNOBSERVABLE_BOUNDARY`, plus its receipt/review are committed) instead of\n   the retired exclusion. `REACHABLE_BOUNDARIES`/`UNOBSERVABLE_BOUNDARY`\n   themselves are untouched — other tests still rely on their values.\n2. `test_a_fresh_episode_executes_the_bootstrap_spine_once_through_langgraph`\n   — a real, reproducible LangGraph `stream(stream_mode=\"updates\")` artifact:\n   the chunk for a step whose *next* step's routing raises in the same tick\n   (the clean one-unit episode's second `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` call, which\n   correctly finds the manifest exhausted and routes to the still-deferred\n   `D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE`) is never yielded, so\n   `result[\"trace\"]`'s `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` count undercounts by exactly\n   one in this case. Fixed by asserting the real, checkpointed final state\n   directly (`state[\"selected_unit_id\"] is None`,\n   `state[\"cursor\"][\"accepted_ordinal\"] == 1`,\n   `\"U001\" in state[\"accepted_unit_receipts\"]`) instead of inferring the\n   outcome from a trace count this specific stream/exception interaction\n   cannot reliably produce. `compiled.stream()`'s call, mode, and\n   `graph.py`/`unit_graph.py` are untouched — only the test's own assertion\n   changed.\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` calls D16-D23's functions\ndirectly against hand-built `FactoryState` fixtures merged through the real\nfield reducers (`state.FIELD_REDUCERS`), and (new in this generation, per\nP-N31-001's required proof) also drives the real compiled production graph\nend to end via the fake-CLI-transport/scripted-response harness\n`test_plan26_unit_graph.py` established (`UG._build_episode_fixture`,\n`UG._run_episode`, `UG._HarnessContext`, `UG._prepare_episode`,\n`UG._scripted_model_context`), imported and reused, not duplicated.\n\n## Owner / retest map\n\n| Owner | Channel | Repair route | First retest node |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| source interpretation | domain | model (M06) | `D07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES` |\n| curriculum domain | domain | model (M06) | `D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN` |\n| unit content | content | model (M06) | `D09_VALIDATE_CONTENT` |\n| unit visual | visuals | model (M06) unless every named key is an authoritative/library brief, then deterministic | `D10_COMPILE_VISUAL_BRIEFS` |\n| unit layout | layout | deterministic (boundary-scoped pointer correction) | `D13_RENDER_UNIT` |\n\n`repair.RETEST_ORDER_BY_OWNER` carries each owner's full fixed chain (spec\nsection 12's table); D21 dispatches only the first node of that chain — the\nremaining steps are the already-wired unit-path edges (N30) that node's own\nsuccess guard reaches on its own, so D21 is never re-entered for the same\nrepair admission.\n\nFrozen limits, enforced exactly where spec section 6.2 assigns them: D17\nowns the repeated-fingerprint bound (`MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS = 2`); D18 owns\nthe numeric attempt bound (`MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = 3`).\n\n## Denominator trace (D16 / D22, `acceptance.compute_unit_denominator`)\n\nRecomputed identically by D16 (before repair) and D22 (immediately before\nminting an accepted receipt) off whatever heads are *current* at call time.\nCategories enforced: source admission (sha256-resolved), domain check set\n(`DOMAIN_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), content check set\n(`CONTENT_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), visual join result,\npage inventory + inspection set (exact page count, all PASS), one\nindependent unit review with every blocking finding's `category` mapped\nthrough the code-owned `owner_for_review_category()` table (never trusted\nverbatim from the model), and repair-request closure (no request left\nunresolved). `test_removing_or_failing_any_single_member_makes_d22_reject`\nindependently removes/fails each of the five owner-bearing categories and\nconfirms D22 raises every time; `test_staling_the_content_head_makes_d22_reject`\nconfirms a check recorded against a superseded head is invisible to the\nreduction (stale evidence cannot pass) — `compute_unit_denominator` only\ncounts a check whose `head_hash` equals the *current* head.\n\nDocumented, not silently assumed, scope limit: the denominator treats the\nappend-only evidence/log layer and the LangGraph checkpoint layer as\nstructurally present (state reducers already enforce their shape) rather\nthan independently re-auditing their hash chain from inside D22 (spec\nsection 13.1 items 13-14). `acceptance.py`'s module docstring records this.\n\n## Compiled-graph proof (P-N31-001 required proof)\n\nAll of the following execute the real compiled graph\n(`graph.build_curriculum_factory_graph(...)`) — never a declared table alone,\nmatching how N90's own audit checked for the defect:\n\n- `test_d16_through_d23_and_m06_are_members_of_the_compiled_production_graph`:\n  D16-D23 and M06 are all members of `compiled.get_graph().nodes`.\n- `test_binding_inventory_return_value_is_unchanged_by_this_nodes_wiring`:\n  `binding_inventory()`'s return value stays disjoint from D16-D23's bodies;\n  `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` is exactly that set plus them.\n- `test_the_six_n31_owned_deferred_edges_are_now_real_wired_edges`: each of\n  the six `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows owned by `N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE`\n  is a real edge in `compiled_topology(compiled)[\"edges\"]`.\n- `test_widening_the_bindings_raises_no_topology_or_binding_error`: a real\n  build against the widened bindings raises no `GraphBindingError`/\n  `UnitTopologyError`.\n- `test_a_clean_one_unit_episode_reaches_d22_accept_unit_via_the_d16_pass_fast_path`:\n  a real run reaches `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE` (pass, no repair),\n  `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`, and `D23_CHECKPOINT_ACCEPTED_UNIT`, with a real minted\n  receipt and `cursor.accepted_ordinal == 1`.\n- `test_a_full_d17_through_d21_repair_and_retest_loop_reaches_d22_accept_unit`:\n  a seeded `layout_repairable` finding drives a real\n  `D17 -> D18 -> D19 -> D20 -> D21 -> D13 (retest) -> D16 -> D22 -> D23` loop\n  over the same compiled graph, closing back to acceptance.\n- Independent evidence dump:\n  `results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/compiled_graph_topology.txt`\n  (node membership, the six wired edges, `binding_inventory()` disjointness,\n  and a graph digest/node-count/edge-count self-check: 42 nodes, 137 edges).\n\n## Real-D98 traces (TEST 9)\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` imports\n`runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal` unmodified and calls\n`terminal.write_terminal()` directly — the identical function N22 wrote and\nN32 will call for its two product-terminal sites — never a stand-in:\n\n- `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_traverses_the_real_d98_and_is_accepted`:\n  a `UNIT_ACCEPTED` candidate built from real D22/D23 output is\n  independently re-derived and accepted by D98's own `_validate_unit_accepted`.\n- `test_a_tampered_unit_accepted_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`: the\n  same candidate with a forged `receipt_hash` is rejected and D98 writes\n  `SYSTEM_FAILURE` in its place — no N31 code decided that; D98's own\n  re-derivation did.\n- `test_a_convergence_exhausted_candidate_from_d17_traverses_the_real_d98`:\n  the `terminal_candidate` D18 proposes on attempt-bound exhaustion is\n  independently accepted by D98's `_validate_exhausted`.\n\nNo test in this file, and no code in `repair.py`/`acceptance.py`, writes to\n`nodes/terminal.py`; `terminal.write_terminal.__module__` is asserted to\nstill be `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal`.\n\n## Commands and results\n\n```\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py -v\n=> 38 passed in 0.81s\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/focused_test_run.txt)\n\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py -v\n=> 93 passed in 7.14s\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/unit_graph_test_run.txt)\n\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest tests/runtime/ -k plan26 -q\n=> 1 failed, 1066 passed, 1 skipped, 174 deselected, 345 subtests passed\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/full_plan26_suite.txt)\n```\n\nBoth of this node's required verification commands are fully green. The one\nbroader-suite failure —\n`test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py::test_passed_nodes_remain_admissible_after_harness_or_predecessor_change`\n— asserts `N20_GRAPH_COMPILER`'s PASSED receipt stays admissible against the\ncurrent on-disk `results/v3/*.receipt.v1.json`/`results/v3/logs/**`\nevidence. It is controller/receipt-evidence state, not a `repair.py`/\n`acceptance.py`/`graph.py` defect: neither this generation nor any test file\nthis node owns writes to `prompt_graph_controller.py` or any receipt file,\nand `N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE`'s declared writable-paths set does not include\nthem.\n\n## Hashes\n\n| File | SHA-256 (shasum -a 256) |\n|---|---|\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py` | `976b47410a001b58b9b5c8be62b2bda21ea2fce0feed5744a953d0ae4b05bb23` |\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py` | `9752736b326e0d58c42affd2166177c42cc0db74626e2b4d83783c8024be1bed` |\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py` | `75d632f51a65ee6e313d0e79366012f166fb37f71534c6c6dcf1912d3348995a` |\n| `tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` | `de6552e7f6d419405ae2cceb619087cc07bf358cc72a6a006cb17b2e3c769385` |\n| `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` | `db62b49c511cea3cc72e6427fdda0fb356f22e5be5dcb00cc6c3a91f4885e54d` |\n\n## TEST item verdicts\n\n1. **PASSED** — `test_d17_rejects_a_finding_with_no_owner`,\n   `test_d17_rejects_a_finding_with_an_unknown_owner`,\n   `test_d17_partitions_a_multi_owner_findings_list_into_separate_owner_entries`,\n   `test_review_finding_category_is_never_trusted_as_an_owner`.\n2. **PASSED** — `test_a_correctly_scoped_model_repair_admits`,\n   `test_a_broad_repair_outside_its_boundary_is_refused`,\n   `test_an_in_place_no_op_repair_is_refused`,\n   `test_a_stale_parent_repair_is_refused`,\n   `test_a_deterministic_layout_repair_changes_only_its_allowed_pointer`.\n3. **PASSED** — `test_attempt_bound_exhausts_before_a_fourth_repair_child`,\n   `test_fingerprint_repeat_bound_exhausts_at_d17`.\n4. **PASSED** — `test_d21_dispatches_the_first_retest_node_of_the_owners_fixed_chain`,\n   `test_stale_evidence_at_an_old_head_cannot_pass_the_denominator`.\n5. **PASSED** — `test_d22_accepts_a_fully_passing_denominator`,\n   `test_removing_or_failing_any_single_member_makes_d22_reject` (×5),\n   `test_staling_the_content_head_makes_d22_reject`.\n6. **PASSED** — `test_accept_once_refuses_a_differing_second_write_for_the_same_unit`,\n   `test_an_already_accepted_unit_can_never_re_enter_classification_or_planning`.\n7. **PASSED** — `test_d23_writes_checkpoint_metadata_and_cursor_in_the_same_update`,\n   `test_d23_refuses_to_advance_the_cursor_with_no_accepted_receipt`.\n8. **PASSED** — `test_coverage_proof_rejects_missing_extra_reordered_and_wrong_hash`.\n9. **PASSED** — `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_traverses_the_real_d98_and_is_accepted`,\n   `test_a_tampered_unit_accepted_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`,\n   `test_a_convergence_exhausted_candidate_from_d17_traverses_the_real_d98`,\n   plus the compiled-graph proof tests above (real one-mode-success and\n   repair-loop runs reach `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT` through the real N22-owned D98\n   path; no N31 write to `terminal.py`).\n10. **PASSED** — `test_repeating_d22_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`,\n    `test_repeating_d23_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`,\n    `test_re_admitting_the_same_repair_after_the_head_already_advanced_fails_closed`,\n    `test_a_crash_before_the_terminal_write_still_lets_d98_be_invoked_cleanly`.\n\n## Residual failures (closed)\n\nGeneration 3 reported `BLOCKED` and honestly named two\n`test_plan26_unit_graph.py` failures caused by this node's own D16-D23\nwiring (per P-N31-002's own instruction not to force a `PASSED` status over\na real residual). P-N31-003 extended this node's write set to\n`test_plan26_unit_graph.py` for exactly those two tests; both are now fixed\n(see \"P-N31-003 correction\" above) and `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` passes\n93/93. No other test in that file was touched.\n\n## Known scope limitations (for N32 and future generations)\n\n- The deterministic-vs-model routing table for `source interpretation` is\n  simplified to always route to M06; spec section 12 allows a deterministic\n  refetch when a locator remains authorized, which would require a\n  source-retrieval integration outside this node's write set\n  (`repair.py`'s module docstring records the reasoning).\n- `compute_unit_denominator()`'s coverage of spec section 13.1 items 13-14\n  (append-log/evidence-index and checkpoint/state-digest integrity) is\n  structural, not a byte-level hash-chain re-audit from inside D22.\n- D24-D32 (N32's workbook engine) remain absent from\n  `build_curriculum_factory_graph`'s compile point; `register_workbook_\n  topology` is defined but not yet called from there. That wiring, and any\n  further widening of `full_binding_inventory()`'s use at the compile point,\n  is N32's write, per `implementation.graph.v3.yaml` and\n  `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md`. This node did not touch `unit_graph.py`,\n  `workbook.py`, or any D24-D32 code.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":11,"newStart":3,"newLines":12,"lines":[" status: PASSED"," node_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N31_repair_acceptance.prompt.v2.md"," predecessor: N30_UNIT_GRAPH (compact state supplied by the controller, status PASSED)","-generation: 1","+generation: 4","+patches_applied: P-N31-001, P-N31-002, P-N31-003"," "," ## What this node built"," ","-Two new top-level modules, per `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md` (\"N31 owns","+Two top-level modules, per `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md` (\"N31 owns"," repair/acceptance modules, not terminal.py\"):"," "," - `runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py` — D17 (finding classification), D18"]},{"oldStart":15,"oldLines":34,"newStart":16,"newLines":103,"lines":["   (boundary-checked admission), D21 (retest dispatch)."," - `runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py` — D16 (unit denominator","   reduction), D22 (recompute-and-accept), D23 (checkpoint correlation +","-  cursor advance), plus `prove_exact_manifest_coverage()`, the D24 coverage","-  predicate N32 will call.","+  cursor advance), `prove_exact_manifest_coverage()` (the D24 coverage","+  predicate N32 calls), and (per P-N31-001) `register_unit_repair_path()`,","+  the additive registration function that wires D16-D23's internal loop over","+  an already-skeleton-registered `StateGraph` builder."," ","-Neither module is registered into the compiled graph yet. `routing.py`'s","-guard tables for D16-D23 already exist (built by N20) and this generation's","-functions emit exactly the guard values those tables declare","-(`unit_denominator_passed`/`unit_findings_repairable`,","-`partition_complete`/`convergence_exhausted`, `repair_planned`,","-`model_repair`/`deterministic_repair`, `repair_admitted`,","-`retest_frontier_incomplete`/`retest_frontier_complete`, `unit_accepted`,","-`checkpoint_correlated`) — but `add_node`/`add_conditional_edges` wiring","-these into `graph.py`'s `StateGraph` is N32's write","-(`implementation.graph.v3.yaml`: N32 owns `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py`,","-N31 does not). Every function here is therefore a plain, narrowly-scoped","-`(state, runtime_context) -> update` callable in the same shape N23's","-`model_nodes.py` already uses for D90/D91 — not wrapped in","-`nodes.deterministic_node()`, since that decorator requires a","-`NODE_CATALOGUE` row this generation is not permitted to add (`nodes/__init__.py`","-is not in N31's write set). A future node binds these to catalogue rows","-without changing this module's bodies.","+Generation 1 left both modules unregistered — real, function-level tested,","+but never `add_node`/`add_conditional_edges`-wired into the one production","+compiled graph. **P-N31-001 correction** (N90 finding F1): `graph.py` is now","+also in this node's write set specifically to close that gap. What changed:"," ","-`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` calls every function","-directly against hand-built `FactoryState` fixtures, merged step-to-step","-through the real field reducers (`state.FIELD_REDUCERS`), not a mock merge.","+- `graph.py` gained `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` (= `binding_inventory()`","+  plus `acceptance.UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES`) and `full_binding_inventory()`","+  (= that, plus N32's still-deferred `workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES`).","+  `binding_inventory()` itself is untouched — its return value is asserted","+  disjoint from `acceptance.UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES` by","+  `test_binding_inventory_return_value_is_unchanged_by_this_nodes_wiring`, so","+  `test_plan26_unit_graph.py`'s own tests, which recompute expectations","+  directly from that function's return value, are unaffected.","+- `graph.py` gained `register_unit_repair_topology(builder, available)`, a","+  thin wrapper that calls `acceptance.register_unit_repair_path(builder,","+  available)` — the same additive-registration-over-an-already-built-builder","+  pattern `workbook.register_workbook_path`/`register_workbook_topology`","+  already established for D24-D32.","+- `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` now compiles against","+  `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` (not the narrower `binding_inventory()`)","+  and calls `register_unit_repair_topology(builder, sorted(bindings))`","+  immediately after `register_skeleton(builder, bindings)` returns. D24-D32","+  stay absent from the compile point; `register_workbook_topology` is still","+  not called from here (unchanged, N32's write).","+- `graph.py`'s `DEFERRED_TOPOLOGY` table gained explicit rows for","+  D18-D23/M06 naming `N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE` as owner, and its module","+  docstring was corrected to describe this generation's compile-point","+  responsibility instead of only the pre-N31 skeleton scope.","+- Neither `unit_graph.py` nor `workbook.py` was touched. The six","+  `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows N31 owns (`D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN ->`,","+  `D09_VALIDATE_CONTENT ->`, `D12_VISUAL_BARRIER_AND_JOIN ->`,","+  `D14_INVENTORY_AND_INSPECT_UNIT_PAGES -> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS`,","+  `D91_CLASSIFY_MODEL_FAILURE -> D17_CLASSIFY_UNIT_FINDINGS`,","+  `M05_REVIEW_ACTUAL_UNIT -> D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE`) resolved","+  automatically, exactly as `unit_graph.register_unit_path` was already","+  designed to do, once D16-D23's bodies entered the bindings it receives —","+  confirmed by compiling and inspecting the real graph, not by re-reading","+  source (see \"Compiled-graph proof\" below)."," ","+**P-N31-002 correction**: generation 2/3's own result report used a","+malformed multi-line `status:` field with a trailing parenthetical, which","+the controller's `^status:\\s*(PASSED|NOT_AVAILABLE|BLOCKED)\\s*$` parser","+cannot match. Fixed to a bare `status: PASSED` line (above); the caveat that","+parenthetical was capturing — stale N20/N30 fixtures — was independently","+resolved by P-N20-001/P-N30-001, and both of this node's required","+verification commands are reconfirmed green below.","+","+**P-N31-003 correction**: generation 3's honest `BLOCKED` report (per","+P-N31-002's own instruction to report a real residual failure rather than","+force a `PASSED` status) named two `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` failures that","+were structural *consequences* of this node's own D16-D23 wiring. Both are","+now closed, in `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` only, nothing else in that file","+touched:","+","+1. `test_the_unobservable_boundary_is_excluded_for_a_stated_reason` — its","+   docstring pre-assigned this rewrite to N31: before D16-D23 were wired,","+   M05's own stream update was swallowed because the branch reaching it","+   resolved to the still-deferred `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE` and aborted the","+   superstep. With D16 now a real node body, M05's update is genuinely","+   observable, so the test now asserts that inversion directly (a real,","+   non-empty `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE`-preceding stream chunk for","+   `UNOBSERVABLE_BOUNDARY`, plus its receipt/review are committed) instead of","+   the retired exclusion. `REACHABLE_BOUNDARIES`/`UNOBSERVABLE_BOUNDARY`","+   themselves are untouched — other tests still rely on their values.","+2. `test_a_fresh_episode_executes_the_bootstrap_spine_once_through_langgraph`","+   — a real, reproducible LangGraph `stream(stream_mode=\"updates\")` artifact:","+   the chunk for a step whose *next* step's routing raises in the same tick","+   (the clean one-unit episode's second `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` call, which","+   correctly finds the manifest exhausted and routes to the still-deferred","+   `D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE`) is never yielded, so","+   `result[\"trace\"]`'s `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` count undercounts by exactly","+   one in this case. Fixed by asserting the real, checkpointed final state","+   directly (`state[\"selected_unit_id\"] is None`,","+   `state[\"cursor\"][\"accepted_ordinal\"] == 1`,","+   `\"U001\" in state[\"accepted_unit_receipts\"]`) instead of inferring the","+   outcome from a trace count this specific stream/exception interaction","+   cannot reliably produce. `compiled.stream()`'s call, mode, and","+   `graph.py`/`unit_graph.py` are untouched — only the test's own assertion","+   changed.","+","+`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` calls D16-D23's functions","+directly against hand-built `FactoryState` fixtures merged through the real","+field reducers (`state.FIELD_REDUCERS`), and (new in this generation, per","+P-N31-001's required proof) also drives the real compiled production graph","+end to end via the fake-CLI-transport/scripted-response harness","+`test_plan26_unit_graph.py` established (`UG._build_episode_fixture`,","+`UG._run_episode`, `UG._HarnessContext`, `UG._prepare_episode`,","+`UG._scripted_model_context`), imported and reused, not duplicated.","+"," ## Owner / retest map"," ","-| Owner | Channel | Repair route (this generation) | First retest node |","+| Owner | Channel | Repair route | First retest node |"," |---|---|---|---|"," | source interpretation | domain | model (M06) | `D07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES` |"," | curriculum domain | domain | model (M06) | `D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN` |"]},{"oldStart":58,"oldLines":21,"newStart":128,"newLines":16,"lines":[" "," Frozen limits, enforced exactly where spec section 6.2 assigns them: D17"," owns the repeated-fingerprint bound (`MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS = 2`); D18 owns","-the numeric attempt bound (`MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = 3`). An earlier","-draft of this generation checked both bounds in D17, which made","-`test_attempt_bound_exhausts_before_a_fourth_repair_child` fail (D17 was","-exhausting a case the prompt's own TEST item expects D18 to exhaust) — fixed","-by removing the attempt-bound check from D17, per spec's own row split (\"D17","-... repeated bound = exhaustion\" vs. \"D18 ... attempt bound = exhaustion\").","+the numeric attempt bound (`MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = 3`)."," "," ## Denominator trace (D16 / D22, `acceptance.compute_unit_denominator`)"," "," Recomputed identically by D16 (before repair) and D22 (immediately before"," minting an accepted receipt) off whatever heads are *current* at call time.","-Categories enforced this generation: source admission (sha256-resolved),","-domain check set (`DOMAIN_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), content","-check set (`CONTENT_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), visual join","-result, page inventory + inspection set (exact page count, all PASS), one","+Categories enforced: source admission (sha256-resolved), domain check set","+(`DOMAIN_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), content check set","+(`CONTENT_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), visual join result,","+page inventory + inspection set (exact page count, all PASS), one"," independent unit review with every blocking finding's `category` mapped"," through the code-owned `owner_for_review_category()` table (never trusted"," verbatim from the model), and repair-request closure (no request left"]},{"oldStart":80,"oldLines":17,"newStart":145,"newLines":45,"lines":[" independently removes/fails each of the five owner-bearing categories and"," confirms D22 raises every time; `test_staling_the_content_head_makes_d22_reject`"," confirms a check recorded against a superseded head is invisible to the","-reduction (stale evidence cannot pass) without needing to delete anything —","-`compute_unit_denominator` only counts a check whose `head_hash` equals the","-*current* head.","+reduction (stale evidence cannot pass) — `compute_unit_denominator` only","+counts a check whose `head_hash` equals the *current* head."," ","-Documented, not silently assumed, scope limit: this generation's denominator","-treats the append-only evidence/log layer and the LangGraph checkpoint layer","-as structurally present (state reducers already enforce their shape) rather","+Documented, not silently assumed, scope limit: the denominator treats the","+append-only evidence/log layer and the LangGraph checkpoint layer as","+structurally present (state reducers already enforce their shape) rather"," than independently re-auditing their hash chain from inside D22 (spec","-section 13.1 items 13-14). `acceptance.py`'s module docstring records this so","-a future generation tightens it rather than rediscovering the gap.","+section 13.1 items 13-14). `acceptance.py`'s module docstring records this."," ","+## Compiled-graph proof (P-N31-001 required proof)","+","+All of the following execute the real compiled graph","+(`graph.build_curriculum_factory_graph(...)`) — never a declared table alone,","+matching how N90's own audit checked for the defect:","+","+- `test_d16_through_d23_and_m06_are_members_of_the_compiled_production_graph`:","+  D16-D23 and M06 are all members of `compiled.get_graph().nodes`.","+- `test_binding_inventory_return_value_is_unchanged_by_this_nodes_wiring`:","+  `binding_inventory()`'s return value stays disjoint from D16-D23's bodies;","+  `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` is exactly that set plus them.","+- `test_the_six_n31_owned_deferred_edges_are_now_real_wired_edges`: each of","+  the six `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows owned by `N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE`","+  is a real edge in `compiled_topology(compiled)[\"edges\"]`.","+- `test_widening_the_bindings_raises_no_topology_or_binding_error`: a real","+  build against the widened bindings raises no `GraphBindingError`/","+  `UnitTopologyError`.","+- `test_a_clean_one_unit_episode_reaches_d22_accept_unit_via_the_d16_pass_fast_path`:","+  a real run reaches `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE` (pass, no repair),","+  `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`, and `D23_CHECKPOINT_ACCEPTED_UNIT`, with a real minted","+  receipt and `cursor.accepted_ordinal == 1`.","+- `test_a_full_d17_through_d21_repair_and_retest_loop_reaches_d22_accept_unit`:","+  a seeded `layout_repairable` finding drives a real","+  `D17 -> D18 -> D19 -> D20 -> D21 -> D13 (retest) -> D16 -> D22 -> D23` loop","+  over the same compiled graph, closing back to acceptance.","+- Independent evidence dump:","+  `results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/compiled_graph_topology.txt`","+  (node membership, the six wired edges, `binding_inventory()` disjointness,","+  and a graph digest/node-count/edge-count self-check: 42 nodes, 137 edges).","+"," ## Real-D98 traces (TEST 9)"," "," `tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` imports"]},{"oldStart":99,"oldLines":9,"newStart":192,"newLines":8,"lines":[" N32 will call for its two product-terminal sites — never a stand-in:"," "," - `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_traverses_the_real_d98_and_is_accepted`:","-  a `UNIT_ACCEPTED` candidate built from this generation's real D22/D23","-  output is independently re-derived and accepted by D98's own","-  `_validate_unit_accepted`.","+  a `UNIT_ACCEPTED` candidate built from real D22/D23 output is","+  independently re-derived and accepted by D98's own `_validate_unit_accepted`."," - `test_a_tampered_unit_accepted_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`: the","   same candidate with a forged `receipt_hash` is rejected and D98 writes","   `SYSTEM_FAILURE` in its place — no N31 code decided that; D98's own"]},{"oldStart":117,"oldLines":36,